#!/usr/bin/env python3
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
#
#   ferry-airc build LIBRARY.metallib -o LIBRARY.dylib
#   ferry-airc list LIBRARY.metallib
#
# Runs a precompiled Metal library on Ferry's software renderer. A
# .metallib that an app ships holds its shaders as LLVM bitcode (one module
# per function, each in LLVM's standard bitcode wrapper), compiled for
# Apple's GPUs. LLVM's own tools read that bitcode, so this script has
# clang turn each module into LLVM's text form, rewrites it for this
# computer's processor, and builds it into the same kind of library
# ferry-mslc makes from source (freemac 1.268):
#
#   - each built-in GPU function the shader calls (maths, conversions,
#     derivatives, texture sampling) gets a body: an LLVM intrinsic, a C
#     library call, or a call into Metal.framework (ferry_metal_abi.h)
#   - each vertex, fragment and kernel function gets the wrapper and info
#     function Metal.framework calls (__ferry_vs_NAME and so on), read from
#     the description each module carries of its entry function: which
#     arguments are buffers, textures, built-in values or stage inputs, and
#     which results go where
#
# clang and ld64.lld (packages clang and lld) do the compiling, as for
# ferry-mslc. A shader that calls a GPU function this script doesn't know
# yet fails to build, and the message names the function.

